  - Valid / invalid cases:
    - Missing file-level @supports template (REQ-TEST-FIX-TEMPLATE, REQ-TEST-FIX-PLACEHOLDER, REQ-TEST-FIX-SAFE, REQ-TEST-FIX-PRESERVE, REQ-TEST-FIX-NO-INFERENCE):
      - Invalid case:
        - `code: describe('Story 020.0-DEV-TEST-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION', () => { it('[REQ-ONE] works', () => {}); });`
        - `output:`
          ```js
          /**
           * @supports docs/stories/XXX.X-STORY-NAME.story.md REQ-XXX-YYY REQ-XXX-ZZZ
           * TODO: Replace the placeholder story path and REQ-IDs with real values for this test file.
           */
          describe('Story 020.0-DEV-TEST-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION', () => { it('[REQ-ONE] works', () => {}); });
          ```
        - `errors: [{ messageId: "missingFileSupports" }]`
    - Malformed prefix spacing (REQ-TEST-FIX-PREFIX-FORMAT):
      - Before: `it('[ REQ-TEST-FIX ] does something', () => {});`
      - After:  `it('[REQ-TEST-FIX] does something', () => {});`
    - Malformed underscore delimiter (REQ-TEST-FIX-PREFIX-FORMAT):
      - Before: `it('[REQ_TEST_FIX] does something', () => {});`
      - After:  `it('[REQ-TEST-FIX] does something', () => {});`
    - Malformed lowercase (REQ-TEST-FIX-PREFIX-FORMAT):
      - Before: `it('[req-lowercase] bad casing', () => {});`
      - After:  `it('[REQ-LOWERCASE] bad casing', () => {});`
    - Malformed parentheses (REQ-TEST-FIX-PREFIX-FORMAT):
      - Before: `it('(REQ-PAREN) with parens', () => {});`
      - After:  `it('[REQ-PAREN] with parens', () => {});`
    - Case with already-correct prefix is left unchanged (safety / preservation):
      - Valid example: `it('[REQ-TRACE-123] behaves correctly', () => {});`
- Test run (via `npm test -- --runInBand --verbose`) shows:
  - `PASS tests/rules/require-test-traceability.test.ts`
  - Overall: `Test Suites: 39 passed, 39 total; Tests: 299 passed, 299 total`.

IMPLEMENTATION – RULE & HELPERS:
- Rule definition: `src/rules/require-test-traceability.ts`
  - Options type includes exactly the configuration described in the story:
    ```ts
    type TestTraceabilityOptions = {
      testFilePatterns?: string[];
      requireDescribeStory?: boolean;
      requireTestReqPrefix?: boolean;
      describePattern?: string;
      autoFixTestTemplate?: boolean;
      autoFixTestPrefixFormat?: boolean;
      testSupportsTemplate?: string;
    };
    ```
  - ESLint metadata declares auto-fix support:
    - `meta.fixable: "code"`
  - Default option values match story expectations:
    - `autoFixTestTemplate: { type: "boolean", default: true }`
    - `autoFixTestPrefixFormat: { type: "boolean", default: true }`
  - create(): integration with helpers and options:
    ```ts
    const {
      testFilePatterns = ["/tests/", "/test/", "/__tests__", ".test.", ".spec."],
      requireDescribeStory = true,
      requireTestReqPrefix = true,
      describePattern = "Story [0-9]+\\.[0-9]+-",
      autoFixTestTemplate = true,
      autoFixTestPrefixFormat = true,
      testSupportsTemplate,
    } = rawOptions as TestTraceabilityOptions;

    const isTestFile = determineIsTestFile(filename, testFilePatterns);
    if (!isTestFile) return {};

    const sourceCode = context.getSourceCode();
    ensureFileSupportsAnnotation(context, sourceCode, {
      autoFixTestTemplate,
      testSupportsTemplate,
    });

    const describeRegex = new RegExp(describePattern);

    return {
      CallExpression: handleCallExpression(context, {
        sourceCode,
        describeRegex,
        requireDescribeStory,
        requireTestReqPrefix,
        autoFixTestPrefixFormat,
      }),
    };
    ```
  - Traceability annotations reference this story and its requirements:
    ```ts
    /**
     * Enforce traceability conventions in test files.
     *
     * @story docs/stories/020.0-DEV-TEST-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION.story.md
     * ...
     * @supports docs/stories/021.0-DEV-TEST-ANNOTATION-AUTO-FIX.story.md REQ-TEST-FIX-TEMPLATE REQ-TEST-FIX-PREFIX-FORMAT REQ-TEST-FIX-SAFE REQ-TEST-FIX-PRESERVE REQ-TEST-FIX-PLACEHOLDER REQ-TEST-FIX-NO-INFERENCE
     */
    ```

- Helper implementation: `src/rules/helpers/require-test-traceability-helpers.ts`
  - File-level template construction (REQ-TEST-FIX-TEMPLATE, REQ-TEST-FIX-PLACEHOLDER):
    ```ts
    function buildSupportsTemplateComment(customTemplate?: string): string {
      const baseTemplate =
        (customTemplate && customTemplate.trim()) ||
        "@supports docs/stories/XXX.X-STORY-NAME.story.md REQ-XXX-YYY REQ-XXX-ZZZ";

      const lines = [
        "/**",
        ` * ${baseTemplate}`,
        " * TODO: Replace the placeholder story path and REQ-IDs with real values for this test file.",
        " */",
        "",
      ];

      return lines.join("\n");
    }
    ```
  - Safe insertion preserving shebang and not touching executable code (REQ-TEST-FIX-SAFE, REQ-TEST-FIX-PRESERVE, REQ-TEST-FIX-NO-INFERENCE):
    ```ts
    function insertSupportsTemplate(fixer: any, sourceCode: any, customTemplate?: string) {
      const text: string = sourceCode.text || "";
      let insertIndex = 0;

      if (text.startsWith("#!")) {
        const firstNewline = text.indexOf("\n");
        insertIndex = firstNewline === NOT_FOUND ? text.length : firstNewline + 1;
      }

      const templateComment = buildSupportsTemplateComment(customTemplate);
      return fixer.insertTextBeforeRange([insertIndex, insertIndex], templateComment);
    }
    ```
  - File-level supports enforcement & auto-fix hook (REQ-TEST-FIX-TEMPLATE, REQ-TEST-FIX-SAFE, REQ-TEST-FIX-NO-INFERENCE):
    ```ts
    export function ensureFileSupportsAnnotation(
      context: any,
      sourceCode: any,
      autoFixOptions: TestTraceabilityAutoFixOptions,
    ): void {
      const fileComments = sourceCode.getAllComments() || [];

      const fileHasSupports = fileComments.some((comment: any) =>
        /@supports\b/.test(comment.value || ""),
      );

      if (!fileHasSupports) {
        const node = (fileComments[0] as any) || (sourceCode.ast && (sourceCode.ast as any));

        context.report({
          node,
          messageId: "missingFileSupports",
          fix:
            autoFixOptions.autoFixTestTemplate === false
              ? undefined
              : (fixer: any) =>
                  insertSupportsTemplate(
                    fixer,
                    sourceCode,
                    autoFixOptions.testSupportsTemplate,
                  ),
        });
      }
    }
    ```
  - REQ prefix normalization logic (REQ-TEST-FIX-PREFIX-FORMAT, REQ-TEST-FIX-SAFE, REQ-TEST-FIX-NO-INFERENCE):
    ```ts
    function normalizeReqId(raw: string): string {
      let id = raw.trim().toUpperCase();

      if (!id.startsWith("REQ")) {
        return id;
      }

      let rest = id.slice(REQ_PREFIX_LENGTH);
      rest = rest.replace(/^[-_\s:]+/, "");
      rest = rest.replace(/[\s_]+/g, "-");
      rest = rest.replace(/-+/g, "-");

      return rest ? `REQ-${rest}` : "REQ-";
    }

    function normalizeReqPrefixInDescription(description: string): string | null {
      const canonicalPattern = /^\[REQ-[^\]]+]/;
      if (canonicalPattern.test(description)) {
        return null;
      }

      const squareMatch = description.match(/^\[\s*(REQ[^\]]*?)\s*](.*)$/i);
      if (squareMatch) {
        const normalizedId = normalizeReqId(squareMatch[1]);
        return `[${normalizedId}]${squareMatch[2] ?? ""}`;
      }

      const parenMatch = description.match(/^\(\s*(REQ[^)]*?)\s*\)(.*)$/i);
      if (parenMatch) {
        const normalizedId = normalizeReqId(parenMatch[1]);
        return `[${normalizedId}]${parenMatch[2] ?? ""}`;
      }

      return null;
    }
    ```
  - Application of prefix normalization in `it`/`test` calls with guarded auto-fix (ensuring only safe cases are fixed and formatting is preserved):
    ```ts
    function handleItOrTestCall(
      context: any,
      node: any,
      description: string,
      options: CallExpressionOptions,
    ): void {
      const { sourceCode, requireTestReqPrefix, autoFixTestPrefixFormat } = options;

      if (!requireTestReqPrefix) return;

      if (!/^\[REQ-[^\]]+]/.test(description)) {
        const normalizedDescription =
          autoFixTestPrefixFormat !== false
            ? normalizeReqPrefixInDescription(description)
            : null;

        context.report({
          node,
          messageId: "missingReqPrefix",
          ...(autoFixTestPrefixFormat !== false &&
            normalizedDescription !== null &&
            node.arguments &&
            node.arguments[0] &&
            node.arguments[0].type === "Literal" &&
            typeof node.arguments[0].value === "string"
              ? {
                  fix(fixer: any) {
                    const literalNode = node.arguments[0];
                    const newRaw = createUpdatedStringLiteralRaw(
                      literalNode,
                      normalizedDescription,
                      sourceCode,
                    );
                    return fixer.replaceText(literalNode, newRaw);
                  },
                }
              : {}),
        });
      }
    }
    ```
  - String-literal update preserves quoting/escaping (REQ-TEST-FIX-PRESERVE):
    ```ts
    function createUpdatedStringLiteralRaw(originalNode: any, newValue: string, sourceCode: any): string {
      const raw = sourceCode.getText(originalNode);
      const firstChar = raw[0];

      if (QUOTES.includes(firstChar as (typeof QUOTES)[number])) {
        const quote = firstChar;
        const escaped = newValue
          .replace(/\\/g, "\\\\")
          .replace(new RegExp(`\\${quote}`, "g"), `\\${quote}`);
        return `${quote}${escaped}${quote}`;
      }

      return JSON.stringify(newValue);
    }
    ```

DOCUMENTATION:
- `user-docs/api-reference.md` includes a dedicated section for `traceability/require-test-traceability` that documents the Story 021.0 auto-fix behavior and template format:
  ```md
  ### traceability/require-test-traceability
  ...
  For Story 021.0, this rule also provides targeted auto-fix capabilities: when run with `--fix`, it can (1) insert a safe, non-semantic file-level `@supports` placeholder template at the top of matching test files when the annotation is missing, including clear TODO guidance for humans to replace the template with a real story and requirement reference, and (2) normalize malformed `[REQ-XXX]` prefixes that already contain an identifiable requirement ID, correcting spacing, bracket/parenthesis usage, underscores, and casing while preserving the original ID text and never inventing new requirement identifiers.
  ```
- Options documented include `autoFixTestTemplate`, `autoFixTestPrefixFormat`, and `testSupportsTemplate`, matching the rule’s option schema and behavior.

